      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-4$ and $z=2.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2).$",
